hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27789","Haddathana Abda ibn Sulayman who said: Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Mamar ibn Abd Allah al-Adawi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None hoards except a sinner."
"27790","Haddathana Yazid: Akhbarana Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Mamar ibn Abd Allah ibn Nadla al-Qurashi who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None hoards except a sinner."
"27791","Haddathana Yaqub who said: Haddathana my father from Ibn Ishaq who said: Haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib al-Misri from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uqba, freedman of Mamar ibn Abd Allah ibn Nafi ibn Nadla al-Adawi, from Mamar ibn Abd Allah who said: I used to saddle for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj; he said: So he said to me one night: O Mamar, tonight I have found disturbance in my girths; he said: So I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I tightened them as I used to tighten them, but one who envied me for my place with you loosened them, to replace me with another; he said: So he said: Indeed I will not do so; he said: So when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed his offering at Mina, he ordered me to shave him; he said: So I took the razor and stood at his head; he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked in my face and said to me: O Mamar, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has enabled you of the lobe of his ear while the razor is in your hand; he said: So I said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, indeed that is of the favor of Allah upon me and His bounty; he said: So he said: Yes, then I affirm for you; he said: Then I shaved the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"27792","Haddathana Hasan who said: Haddathana Ibn Lahia who said: Haddathana Abu al-Nadr that Busr ibn Said told him from Mamar ibn Abd Allah that he sent a slave of his with a sa of wheat and said to him: Sell it, then buy barley with it; so the slave went and took a sa and addition of part of a sa; so when he came to Mamar he informed him of that, so Mamar said to him: Did you do so; go and return it, and take only like for like; for I used to hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Food for food, like for like; and our food that day was barley; it was said: For it is not like it; he said: Indeed I fear it resembles."
"27793","Haddathana Harun who said: Haddathana Ibn Wahb who said: Akhbarani Amr that Abu al-Nadr told him that Busr ibn Said told him from Mamar ibn Abd Allah, and he mentioned its meaning."
